  "verified": [
    "Visual root-type creation, exact decimal field schema, active-owner rule and lifecycle; duplicate-key raw import denial, return to last valid draft, valid import and authored JSON export roundtrip.",
    "Visual child authoring with an exact parent version, explicit copied local override, inherited required ownership and inherited lifecycle. Resolved metadata and immutable dependency pins are read back from the real API.",
    "A real scanned PostgreSQL asset cannot receive the required-owner type without an active owner. UI ownership assignment then succeeds, and ordinary owner removal is rejected without losing the binding.",
    "Legal lifecycle transition is committed; illegal transition returns 422 and leaves the full type-state response unchanged. Reassigning a newer version of the same authored type preserves the active state and exact decimal string.",
    "A parent upgrade leaves existing child definitions/resolution hashes and asset version pins unchanged. An explicit child parent-pin upgrade requires a complete preview and digest-bound consent.",
    "Concurrent canonical asset edit makes publication return 409, leaves the child head unchanged and preserves the draft parent pin. Reload and fresh preview/consent allow compatible publication while prior child versions remain immutable.",
    "Consumers can read permitted type/lifecycle information but cannot author or transition in UI or API. The other tenant sees 404 for foreign type/asset state, empty scoped type search, and can create its own independent same-identifier type.",
    "Authored types link from the model list to their type page. Legacy model edit/migration routes display the authored-type route and expose no misleading publication or migration action.",
    "The existing OIDC/source scan/catalog/ownership/audit, model editor/typed values/pagination, explicit migration/receipt, role/tenant and accessibility journeys all pass in the full ten-test gate."
